WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:07.840
Is this Kurdistan's moment?

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.590
Are they going to finally achieve independence?

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:14.450
You know, if you ask any Kurd that, they're
going to say that they want independence,

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:17.290
but the problem really comes down to the Kurdish
leadership.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:23.480
Masoud Barzani, the leader of Iraqi Kurdistan,
who's now serving the ninth year of his eight-year

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:29.260
presidency, oftentimes tries to rally Kurds
around the flag of Kurdish Nationalism, but

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.120
when push comes to shove, it seems he wants
money more than nationalism.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.839
Remember back in 1996, he invited Saddam Hussein's
forces into the Kurdish capital simply because

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.590
he didn't want another Kurdish rival to take
power.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:48.230
Now, when it comes to the PKK, this group
in Turkey that's waging an insurgency, or

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.120
this group in Syria which has established
as an autonomous region, they're no longer

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:54.350
officially talking about separatism.

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:56.210
They're talking about federalism.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:01:00.820
They're actually talking about what they call
democratic autonomy or confederalism, where

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:06.930
they want a group of Kurdish regions which
overlay other countries.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.340
So what’s your opinion of Kurdish independence?

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.510
Let us know in the comments, and also let
us know what other topics you want us to cover

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.320
here at AEI in sixty seconds.

